# server: /metrics counts the prompt tokens restored from kept prompt states (tensorfold:prompt_tokens_cached_total).
# The engine already knows each request's cached count (it is in the reply's usage.prompt_tokens_details.cached_tokens
# and on the `done ... cached=N` log line) but /metrics published only prompt_tokens_total, so a dashboard could not
# tell cached from computed prefill: on an agent workload where 98.4% of 674 M prompt tokens were restored from the
# prompt cache (3,153 requests, summed from the log), sparkDash showed every token as computed prefill.
# - A backport of upstream ashhart/TensorFold ce0d9053be ("feat(metrics): count prompt tokens restored from kept
#   prompt states", PR #531), which this fork branched before: Info.prompt_cache says the engine keeps prompt states;
#   each finished request adds the cached count its `prefilled` event reported; /metrics then carries
#   tensorfold:prompt_tokens_cached_total and repeats it with prompt_tokens_total as vLLM's prefix_cache_hits_total and
#   prefix_cache_queries_total. An engine that keeps no prompt states leaves all three out, as before. Same names, help
#   text and tests as upstream.
# - Added for this fork: the CUDA host (native/cuda.zig) sets Info.prompt_cache when it built a prompt cache, so the
#   DeepSeek-V4.1 lane publishes the counter (`--prompt-cache-gib 0` leaves it out). Host test: the flag follows the cache.
# Switch: none (always on). Replies and the decode path are unchanged: one integer add per finished request under the
# metrics mutex. The right long-term home is the engine fork: once its branch takes ashhart #531, a repin of TF_REF
# carries this and the patch goes (a repin onto upstream v1.1.x itself is not a drop-in: it serves no DeepSeek-V4.1).
